I will give a brief response to Members speeches on individual issues
National security is within the scope of duties and powers of the Central Authorities
As the countrys supreme authority the National Peoples Congress NPC and its Standing Committee absolutely have the power and responsibility to enact laws for Hong Kong . The National Peoples Congress NPC adopted the Decision on the Added Justice to the Legislation in the 528 Decision to authorize NPCSC to enact the National Security Law to establish a sound legal system and enforcement mechanism for safeguarding national security for Hong Kong to successfully implement one country two systems to unfold a new chapter and to set a new pattern for Hong Kong and to set a new milestone for Hong Kongs development
In fact many countries in the world such as the United States the United Kingdom Australia and Canada have long since enacted specialized laws to safeguard national security
The offences regulated under the National Security Law are similar to those under the national security laws of other countries with the objective of safeguarding national sovereignty territorial integrity and development interests
Article 23 of the Basic Law has not changed the basic principle I have just mentioned . It requires the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region SAR to discharge its constitutional responsibility for legislating for certain offences concerning national security
In fact the Central Authorities have all along been entitled to the legislative power and the duty to deal with national security issues especially when the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region HKSAR has not fulfilled this responsibility
Therefore not only has one country two systems not been changed but it has also been reinforced
The additional effect of the Hong Kong National Security Law is in line with the principle of protection and jurisdiction under the international law
The principle of protection and jurisdiction is also common in several international treaties against terrorism
The laws relating to national security of many countries are also extremely effective . For example the German criminal law against the crime of treason the United States law against collusion of foreign and foreign forces the Law of Logan the Foreign Correctional Services Act and the Singapore law against the use of fake information and cyber manipulation on the Internet
Regarding the appointment of a designated judge I reiterate that the Chief Executive only sets a list of designated judges for courts of different ranks and does not appoint a judge to handle a specific case
When dealing with the relevant cases the judges still perform their judicial functions independently (with out ) being intervened by anyone
Therefore the National Security Law has absolutely not undermined the judicial independence that the Hong Kong SAR has all along been respected in respect of the arrangement for appointing judges
This is also confirmed by the court in the case of TONG Ying – kit
Some Members have also mentioned the relationship between personal interests and (over all ) interests
Article 2 of the National Security Law clearly provides that Article 1 and 12 of the Basic Law are fundamental provisions
Recently some people in the community have criticized the Standing Committee of the National Peoples Congress NPCSC for violating the local judicial system in making decisions on issues relating to Hong Kong
Members should bear in mind that China is a single state and its power comes from the Central Authorities
The Basic Law is an authority and the Constitution and the Basic Law clearly explain the powers and responsibilities of the Central Authorities and the Central Authorities Authorities in the HKSAR
When constitutional issues are involved the Standing Committee of the National Peoples Congress NPCSC has the responsibility powers and it is necessary to make relevant decisions in accordance with the Constitution and the Basic Law to provide a binding legal basis to accurately implement the constitutional order jointly constructed by the Constitution and the Basic Law
It is precisely this lack of understanding or misunderstanding of the Constitution and the Basic Law that prompted the Department of Justice DoJ to organize the 30 Anniversary Legal Advocacy Forum on the Basic Law last year to trace its roots and through expert introduction and sharing enable the general public to have a correct understanding and understanding of the Constitution and the Basic Law
Besides the Department of Justice will continue to promote the work of the Constitution the Basic Law and the National Security Law edit and edit of the Basic Law and produce electronic teaching materials for teachers to teach the Basic Law and the rule of law education as well as launch rule of law pilot schemes for primary and secondary students etc
There are various definitions and interpretations of the rule of law . There are many indicators and there is no universal standard recognized by the international community . But there is one point which is very clear that any claim of achieving justice by violating the law will definitely violate the spirit of the rule of law . These incorrect concepts must be rectified
To uphold the rule of law (every one ) has a responsibility and the whole community must abide by the law and actively promote the correct concept of rule of law
As I have pointed out in my speech at the Commencement Ceremony for the Legal Year 2020 the rule of law is a matter of personal choice and there are some subjective feelings as well as objective indicators
In view of this the Department of Justice is setting up an Objective and Rule of Law Database under the Vision 2030 on Focusing on the Rule of Law for a Ten Year Plan and is now actively preparing and organizing the relevant data
Judicial independence is an important part of the rule of law and Article 85 of the Basic Law safeguards judicial independence
As a guardian of public interests I have the obligation to act in accordance with the rights and obligations conferred by law
Therefore I have applied to the court for four prohibition orders including prohibition of doxxing and harassment of judicial and law enforcement officers
Protection of judicial independence is not only the responsibility of the Government or the Department of Justice but also the obligation of every member of the public
Different people in society especially the two legal professional bodies which are important stakeholders of the legal sector namely The Hong Kong Bar Association and The Law Society of Hong Kong have the responsibility to defend judicial independence in accordance with the Rules of Procedure and the Ordinance respectively
While there are different ways to defend judicial independence it is necessary to spread the right message
Members have also expressed their views on the issue of judicial reform
I hope Members will look at judicial reform with an open mind
As a matter of fact the Judiciary has been conducting continuous reviews . The Chief Justice of the Court of Final Appeal pointed out at the commencement ceremony of the legal year this year that the Judiciary would digitize the legal procedures and support systems review the mechanism for handling complaints against judges and set out the advantages and disadvantages for different types of cases to enhance the efficiency of handling cases
The judicial reform should be led by the Judiciary and the Department of Justice will fully support and complement the enhancement measures of the Judiciary
If someone is dissatisfied with the sentence the existing appeal or review mechanism in the court is effective
The number of criminal review applications submitted by the Department of Justice DoJ this year has substantially increased in comparison with 2019 there were 17 cases in 2020
In 2020 12 applications were ruled valid and 11 were approved
Among the four cases the Court of Appeal reiterated the principle of sentence in the WONG Chee Fung case that is it must emphasize the function of deterrence and punishment in handling large scale unlawful assembly cases involving violence
The Court of Appeal has also pointed out that the principles clarified in the Wong Chi Fung case should be appropriately applied and should not be left to the mouth
A Member has also mentioned the Commission on Torture and Cruelty
Such institutions have many different purposes and functions . Some jurisdictions have set up dedicated institutions to balance the discretionary power of the courts and the consistency of judgments to formulate judgment guidelines . These institutions can be regarded as judicial institutions or independent institutions
In Hong Kong if we are to consider setting up such an organization we must first clarify the problem and then find the right remedy
If there are other reasons as pointed out by the former Chief Justice as long as there are details reasons and justifications I believe the Judiciary will follow up seriously
The Department of Justice will use the Legal Technology Fund to develop the Hong Kong Legal Cloud and entrust an independent third party to manage the Legal and Controversial Service Professionals to subsidize the fees incurred by the Legal and Controversial Service Professionals for using the Hong Kong Legal Cloud in the initial stage
Some Members have also mentioned the development opportunities in the Guangdong Hong Kong and Macao Greater Bay Area GBA
Hong Kong is the only jurisdiction that enforces common law within the country
Under one country two systems and three laws Hong Kongs independent and sound legal system can provide diversified services to enterprises in the Greater Bay Area
Moreover in August 2020 the Shenzhen Economic Special Administrative Region Hengang Shenzhen and Hong Kong Modern Service Industry Cooperation Zones Ordinance was passed to allow Hong Kong enterprises in the Greater Bay Area Wokiee to use Hong Kong laws as contractual applicable laws (with out ) exception
This initiative of taking the lead is a major breakthrough
The Department of Justice is now actively seeking support from the Central Authorities to strive for the implementation of the Hong Kong law for Hong Kong investors in the Greater Bay Area so that Hong Kong enterprises can choose the Hong Kong laws they are familiar with for trading
The above arrangements are the support given by the Central Authorities to Hong Kong with a view to highlighting the unique status and advantages brought by the Basic Law and one country two systems to Hong Kong and strengthening Hong Kongs position as a centre for facilitating transactions and resolving disputes
The Department of Justice has been maintaining close cooperation with international organizations and providing training opportunities for legal talents including arrangements for them to apply for employment with international organizations
After signing the Legal Professionals Umbrella Scheme with the International Council of Justice in Kenya in December last year the Scheme will officially commence in Kenya tomorrow
The Department of Justice has also succeeded in seeking to organize a number of international government meetings in Hong Kong such as the Association of Association of Asian African Lawyers which has been held since the outbreak of the epidemic last year
Deputy President the Constitution and the Basic Law are the constitutional foundations of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region SAR . The SAR Government will continue to firmly uphold the principle of one country two systems in a holistic and consistent manner in accordance with the Constitution and the Basic Law
As the Deputy President has pointed out the original intent of the reunification of Hong Kong with one country two systems is to ensure the joint implementation of the central comprehensive jurisdiction and the high degree of autonomy of the Hong Kong Special Administrative Region so that one country two systems can be established in a stable and orderly manner
The Department of Justice will continue to perform its constitutional functions and strive to uphold the core values of the rule of law and judicial independence in Hong Kong through various policy initiatives
We have listened attentively to Members views and expectations and will actively follow up on the matter as appropriate
I hope Members will continue to support the policies and measures of the Department of Justice and join hands with us in promoting the rule of law and justice and sharing the fruits of prosperity
Thank you President and Honourable Members
